 {
  "type": "tweet",
  "id": "2103904120130195749",
  "url": "https://x.com/ffdataroma/status/2103904120130195749",
  "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/ffdataroma/status/2103904120130195749",
  "text": "DK Metcalf\n\nDK has a really tough matchup in this one, as the Bengals have been quite good defending the perimeter over the past year plus, in large part due to CB1 DJ Turner. They allowed the 6th fewest YPG there in 2025, and have allowed the 9th fewest through 2 weeks of the 2026 season. DK has been out-wide on 80% of his routes this year.\n\nDK, who has been a relatively unimpressive target-earner for most of the past few years (0.22 TPRR since 2024), could struggle to get looks. That could be exacerbated by the Bengals\u2019 frequent 2-high looks (top 12 rate in 2026), where DK drops off from 0.22\u21920.19 TPRR since 2024 per @FantasyPtsData.\n\nThe Bengals have gotten a lot of pressure in 2026 (7th highest), which DK has been notably worse off against. Last year, he tanked from 1.98\u21920.85 YPRR and 0.23\u21920.08 TPRR when PIT was pressured (among the biggest drop-offs of any WR). With a seemingly much improved defense overall too (2nd in NFL in EPA/Play), it could be tough sledding for DK and this whole offense.\n\nThe Play: Under 52.5 rec yards, DFS fade",
